        "original_id": "d4be12ce-451d-520d-8c0c-08edb08cae04",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Centaurium, Dacrydium, Schenkia\n- Taxonomy: Gentianaceae, Chironieae, Chironiinae, Podocarpaceae\n\nFacts:\n- Centaurium, also called centaury, is a plant genus with 20 species in the gentian family Gentianaceae, tribe Chironieae, and subtribe Chironiinae.\n- Dacrydium is a plant genus of conifers in the podocarp family Podocarpaceae.\n- Dacrydium currently has 16 recognized species of evergreen dioecious trees and shrubs.\n- Schenkia is sometimes included in the genus Centaurium.",
